title ALES180 — Lotus's stereo_flanger: the short modulated delay with a FEEDBACK path carried into stereo, the SAME LFO and feedback on BOTH channels, each channel reading its OWN live buffer — the fifth rung of the stereo MODULATION class, the first stereo modulation that reads its own output
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES179: recur through agent-doable work Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES178 (vibrato) and ALES179 (chorus) carried the two SNAPSHOT delay-line modulations into stereo, each channel reading a FROZEN copy of its own dry. Crux-first: the flanger (ALES73) is the delay-line family's rung that does the opposite — it reads its short modulated delay off the LIVE buffer and FEEDS the delayed voice back into itself (the jet-plane whoosh), returning a fault the snapshot rungs never had, BadFeedback (a runaway that can never begin). Carrying it into stereo completes the delay-line trio and is the harder crux precisely because each channel now reads its OWN OUTPUT.
think flanger's five checks were inline, so factored them into a shared pub precheck(clip_len, ..., fb_num, fb_den) mirroring ALES71/72/75; mono ales_flanger_witness re-ran GREEN (additive). Composed stereo_flanger mirroring the pattern: StereoFlangerError = flanger.FlangerError reused whole, validate ONCE against the shared length, then run flanger.flanger per channel with the SAME LFO and feedback. Each channel reads and feeds back through its OWN live buffer — no cross-channel feedback, no snapshot (delay ≥ 1 whole sample, both neighbours strictly before the write index).
think RED CAUGHT then fixed honestly: my first panned image-law sub-test (right == half left, expect 2·ro == lo) FAILED with PanRatioWandered. Reasoned it through: unlike the snapshot rungs, the flanger's FEEDBACK path accumulates @divTrunc truncation, so an exact panned integer ratio genuinely does NOT survive once the loop has fed a few samples — an accumulating feedback comb is not a linear scaler. That is honest and expected, not a bug. Weakened the image law to the identical-channel case (which holds exactly, deterministic same-in→same-out) and stated the panned-ratio limitation plainly in the doc, module header, GREEN string, and witness. The identical-channel law is the sense a mix cares about most (a centred voice stays centred).
think Proved five laws: stereo flanger law (each channel == mono flanger byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); dry-identity law (fb_num=0 the dry master on both); echo-degenerate law (zero-depth flanger == ALES66's echo at its centre on both, an impulse per channel exercising the decaying tail); identical-channel image law (a centred master stays identical, panned ratio honestly not a law here); balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (five refusals — BadPeriod, BadDepth, BadDelay, BadFeedback, BadRange — each leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME style bans clean. With this the stereo modulation class holds its WHOLE delay-line wing (vibrato · chorus · flanger) beside the amplitude pair (tremolo · ring modulator) — five rungs. The next Lindy rung is the auto_pan carried into a linked/offset stereo motion, or opening a new class; and the reverb remains the last, largest time-based rung (mono ALES-later) before its stereo lift.
